<title>UK: India could need sugar imports in 97/98 - Czarnikow.</title>
<headline>India could need sugar imports in 97/98 - Czarnikow.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India could have to import sugar in 1997/98 due to expected production falls, Czarnikow Sugar said in its monthly report on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;One of the major swing factors in the world is India and, not only has the current crop for that country slipped back significantly, but further falls are anticipated for 1997/98, making it likely that imports could be needed in 1997/98,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>It gave no estimate of India's future import requirements.</p>
<p>In February Czarnikow estimated India's sugar production at 15.00 million tonnes raw value in 1996/97, sharply down from its previous forecast of 16.30 million.</p>
<p>Production in 1995/96 totalled 17.88 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
